<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ============================================================================
         CRW v1 BASELINE, part 3 of 3: the published emission-owed contract.

         THIS IS THE VERSION 1 BASELINE. The database is dropped and recreated at the
         v1 cutover, so this runs only against an empty schema. Two guards the
         previous revision carried are deliberately absent:

           - replaceIfExists on the view. It existed so a database where the ORIGINAL
             changeset had already created the view converged instead of failing. No
             such database survives the cutover, and a create that cannot collide does
             not need a replace.
           - the second changeset id. The previous file carried the create twice under
             two ids, because databases holding a MARK_RAN row for the first id had to
             reconsider it. There is no history to reconsider, so there is one id.

         The onFail="CONTINUE" precondition below is NOT scar tissue and STAYS. It is
         the A-79 fix and it guards a condition that is real on an empty v1 database:
         the view spans tables owned by three OTHER services, and CRW's window job
         reaches Liquibase every 10 seconds from cluster start, long before the first
         DC arrival makes CDE create cde_schedule.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <!--
      SCRUM-107: the PUBLISHED contract for "does this arrival still owe Fintegrate
      an emission?". AGT gates DAG_COMPLETE on it, so a collections arrival can no
      longer report complete before CRW has written anything (R-37 as amended).

      Published as a view for the same reason prg_report_due and prg_sla_pending are:
      the completeness RULE is CRW's, so it belongs next to the crw_emission tables
      that decide it. AGT reading crw_emission.state directly would couple it to a
      literal this repo treats as provisional.

      OWED, not EMITTED. That distinction is the whole point, and getting it wrong
      strands arrivals:
        - an arrival with zero PASS rows can never emit, so it owes nothing and must
          be allowed to terminate. Gating it on an emission that will never exist
          leaves it DAG_RUNNING forever (a PARTIAL-mode client with a wholly bad file
          reaches CTV BUSINESS_PARTIAL, not FILE_REJECTED, so it does hit this path);
        - a multi-batch arrival owes until EVERY planned batch is VISIBLE, not until
          the first one is. crw_emission is per (arrival, run_date, batch_ordinal) and
          publication commits one batch at a time, so any-row-visible completes with
          batches still undelivered;
        - a multi-process-date arrival owes until the futured remainder has emitted
          too, which is a later run_date and a different group entirely.

      The view spans tables owned by four services in the shared dcre_col: tx_header
      (CRR), validation_log (CTV), cde_schedule (CDE) and crw_emission/_group (CRW).
      Which of them exist depends on what has run, so the changeset is guarded and
      RETRIED rather than skipped once.

      A-79 (2026-08-07): MARK_RAN does not mean "skip", it means "record as applied,
      permanently". The original changeset MARK_RANed on the very first CRW window,
      before CDE had created cde_schedule, and the view was then never created for the
      life of that database. AGT fails closed to OWED on the missing relation, which
      is the right direction and makes it a SILENT permanent hang: every collections
      arrival sits in DAG_RUNNING forever with no error anywhere. A dependency that
      has not bootstrapped yet is not work already done. CONTINUE is the retryable
      skip: skip this run, record NOTHING, re-evaluate next startup.

      The predicate itself is exercised against a real database by EmissionOwedViewIT,
      which reads the view body out of THIS file so the two cannot drift.
    -->
    <changeSet id="crw-v1-emission-owed-view" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE"
                       onFailMessage="crw_emission_owed not created yet: CRR/CTV/CDE have not all
                       run on this database. Bootstrap ordering, not a failure; retried next run.">
            <tableExists tableName="tx_header"/>
            <tableExists tableName="validation_log"/>
            <tableExists tableName="cde_schedule"/>
            <tableExists tableName="crw_emission_group"/>
        </preConditions>

        <createView viewName="crw_emission_owed" fullDefinition="false">
            SELECT h.arrival_id AS arrival_id,
                   (
                     EXISTS (
                       SELECT 1 FROM cde_schedule s
                       JOIN validation_log v
                         ON v.arrival_id = s.arrival_id AND v.sequence = s.sequence
                       WHERE s.arrival_id = h.arrival_id
                         AND v.outcome = 'PASS'
                         AND s.process_date > current_date
                     )
                     OR EXISTS (
                       SELECT 1 FROM crw_emission_group g
                       WHERE g.arrival_id = h.arrival_id
                         AND g.expected_batch_count > (
                           SELECT count(*) FROM crw_emission e
                           WHERE e.arrival_id = g.arrival_id
                             AND e.run_date = g.run_date
                             AND e.state = 'VISIBLE'
                         )
                     )
                     OR (
                       EXISTS (
                         SELECT 1 FROM validation_log v2
                         WHERE v2.arrival_id = h.arrival_id AND v2.outcome = 'PASS'
                       )
                       AND NOT EXISTS (
                         SELECT 1 FROM crw_emission_group g2
                         WHERE g2.arrival_id = h.arrival_id
                       )
                     )
                   ) AS owed
            FROM tx_header h
        </createView>

        <rollback>
            <dropView viewName="crw_emission_owed"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
